#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105386 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "dcf425bc-d6ce-5cab-87ea-2d4d42270d09" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Vector Equation of a Line Given a Point and Direction Vector"}] :question/id #uuid "9fa21896-8127-5ec5-aff0-7f811403db8c" :question/math-academy-id "e-12442" :question/problem "Find a vector equation of the straight line passing through $P(3,-1,7)$ and parallel to ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073156/assets/48f9afd751f6424fe465e494fd254593de065563231a1f5df07741789969c1af.png)" :question/worked-solution "The vector equation of the straight line passing through $P$ and parallel to $\\mathbf{v}$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{r} = \\mathbf{p} + t \\mathbf{v},\n$$\n\nwhere $t \\in (-\\infty, \\infty)$ and $\\mathbf{p}$ is the position vector of $P$.\n\nIn our case, the position vector of the point $P$ is ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073156/assets/9264ecd5e62e51eec08ae686461f8b3d99aadbddd2363b5c700c72839d59524f.png)\n\nUsing the formula for the vector equation of a line, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105387 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a6dee200-f517-5645-87ec-ccf36012e55e" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Vector Equation of the Line Passing Through Two Given Points"}] :question/id #uuid "d1adb6fb-cd44-5a12-b892-6a6d2c99929d" :question/math-academy-id "e-12443" :question/problem "Find a vector equation of the line that passes through the points $P(1,-1,2)$ and $Q(3,2,7).$" :question/worked-solution "The vector equation of the straight line passing through $P$ and parallel to $\\mathbf{v}$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{r} = \\mathbf{p} + t \\mathbf{v},\n$$\n\nwhere $t \\in (-\\infty, \\infty)$ and $\\mathbf{p}$ is the position vector of $P.$ \n\nWe can find a direction vector by computing the displacement vector between the given points $P(1,-1,2)$ and $Q(3,2,7),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\overset{\\to }{PQ} \\\\  & =⟨3,2,7⟩-⟨1,-1,2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2,3,5⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the vector equation of the line is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105388 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c338d1eb-7e13-5089-8dd3-d5ca6eefd4ba" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Points on a Line That Are a Fixed Distance From Another Point on the Line"}] :question/id #uuid "55ee3b10-087f-521e-ba37-12541e199408" :question/math-academy-id "e-12444" :question/problem "Consider the straight line that passes through $P(1,2,0)$ and parallel to $\\mathbf{v}= \\langle -4,1,1 \\rangle.$ Find all the possible points $A$ on that line such that $PA=6\\sqrt{2}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the vector equation of the line, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =p+tv \\\\ r & =⟨1,2,0⟩+t⟨-4,1,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $t \\in (-\\infty, \\infty).$\n\nSince $A$ lies on the line, we know that there must be a real number $t$ such that\n\n$$\n\\overrightarrow{OA} = \\langle 1, 2, 0 \\rangle + t \\langle -4, 1, 1 \\rangle\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PA} & =\\overset{\\to }{OA}-\\overset{\\to }{OP} \\\\  & =(⟨1,2,0⟩+t⟨-4,1,1⟩)-⟨1,2,0⟩ \\\\  & =t\\,⟨-4,\\,1,\\,1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-4t,\\,t,\\,t⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the fact that $PA=6\\sqrt{2},$ we get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}PA & =6\\sqrt{2} \\\\ |\\overset{\\to }{PA}| & =6\\sqrt{2} \\\\ |⟨-4t,\\,t,\\,t⟩| & =6\\sqrt{2} \\\\ \\sqrt{(-4t)^{2}+{t}^{2}+{t}^{2}} & =6\\sqrt{2} \\\\ \\sqrt{18{t}^{2}} & =6\\sqrt{2} \\\\ \\pm 3t\\sqrt{2} & =6\\sqrt{2} \\\\ t & =\\pm 2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, putting the values $t=\\pm 2$ into the equation for the line, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\overset{\\to }{O{A}_{1}}=⟨1,2,0⟩+2⟨-4,1,1⟩=⟨-7,4,2⟩, \\\\  & \\overset{\\to }{O{A}_{2}}=⟨1,2,0⟩-2⟨-4,1,1⟩=⟨9,0,-2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the points are $A_1(-7, 4, 2)$ and $A_2(9, 0, -2).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105389 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f78fe749-e37e-53f2-879f-4c36931c1d6f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Vector Equation of a Line Segment"}] :question/id #uuid "69c3fc44-8b4d-521e-b207-0ea01d5921e1" :question/math-academy-id "e-12445" :question/problem "Using $\\mathbf{i},\\mathbf{j},\\mathbf{k}$ notation, find a parametrization of the line segment $\\overline{PQ},$ where $P(-4,1,2)$ and $Q(-2,5,-1).$" :question/worked-solution "We need to find a direction vector that is parallel to the given line. We can use the vector $\\overrightarrow{PQ}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\overset{\\to }{PQ} \\\\  & =\\overset{\\to }{OQ}-\\overset{\\to }{OP} \\\\  & =(-2\\,i+5\\,j-k)-(-4\\,i+j+2\\,k) \\\\  & =2\\,i+4\\,j-3\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the vector equation of the line is\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{r} = \\mathbf{p} + t \\mathbf{v} \n\\qquad\\Longrightarrow\\qquad\n\\mathbf{r} = (-4 \\, \\mathbf{i} + \\mathbf{j} + 2\\,\\mathbf{k}) + t (2 \\, \\mathbf{i} + 4 \\, \\mathbf{j} - 3 \\, \\mathbf{k})\n$$\n\nand the parametrization of the line segment $\\overline{PQ}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t) & =(-4\\,i+j+2\\,k)+t(2\\,i+4\\,j-3\\,k) \\\\  & =(2t-4)\\,i+(4t+1)\\,j+(2-3t)\\,k,\\,t\\in [0,1].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186378834 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "dcf425bc-d6ce-5cab-87ea-2d4d42270d09" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Vector Equation of a Line Given a Point and Direction Vector"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c7fba8fc-77d6-5766-8fe9-f9d1c3909258" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨-2,\\,\\frac{3}{5},\\,\\sqrt{5}⟩+t⟨-1,\\,2,\\,3⟩,\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378836} {:answer/id #uuid "d01e8e91-d5f8-5ea6-8602-fea3c6efd8a2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨2,\\,3,\\,-1⟩+⟨\\sqrt{5},\\,\\frac{3}{5},\\,-2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378837} {:answer/id #uuid "184822ad-2e01-53b7-8688-5547d3e59400" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨2,\\,3,\\,-1⟩+t⟨\\sqrt{5},\\,\\frac{3}{5},\\,-2⟩,\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378838} {:answer/id #uuid "c58db8d9-9b95-50a8-a9e5-6ef7e09038fd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨2,\\,-1,\\,3⟩+t⟨\\sqrt{5},\\,-2,\\,\\frac{3}{5}⟩,\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378839} {:answer/id #uuid "608641f9-afb3-5bae-9d25-2a26c115ebb4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨\\sqrt{5},\\,\\frac{3}{5},\\,-2⟩+t⟨2,\\,3,\\,-1⟩,\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378840}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "608641f9-afb3-5bae-9d25-2a26c115ebb4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨\\sqrt{5},\\,\\frac{3}{5},\\,-2⟩+t⟨2,\\,3,\\,-1⟩,\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378840} :answer-field/id #uuid "feadbeec-0f45-58e5-9409-a37ec90ff75a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378835}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "00ffce9f-fde5-5943-bf47-164dc6539869" :question/math-academy-id "q-126431" :question/problem "Find a vector equation of the straight line passing through $Q(\\sqrt{5},\\,\\frac{3}{5},\\,-2)$ and parallel to $v=⟨2,\\,3,\\,-1⟩.$" :question/worked-solution "The vector equation of the straight line passing through $Q$ and parallel to $v$ is given by\n\n$$\nr=q+tv,\n$$\n\nwhere $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )$ and $q$ is the position vector of $Q.$ \n\nIn our case, the position vector of the point $Q$ is $q=⟨\\sqrt{5},\\,\\frac{3}{5},\\,-2⟩.$ \n\nUsing the formula for the vector equation of a line, we have\n\n$$\nr=⟨\\sqrt{5},\\,\\frac{3}{5},\\,-2⟩+t⟨2,\\,3,\\,-1⟩,\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186378841 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a6dee200-f517-5645-87ec-ccf36012e55e" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Vector Equation of the Line Passing Through Two Given Points"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "86fb47a6-9951-5289-a89d-51470953df6b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378843} {:answer/id #uuid "29ff2373-e25a-5d6b-afc4-878204b60ffd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -5 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378844} {:answer/id #uuid "0379a423-f0ae-5fe9-9c4c-3f97e5d9dfe9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378845} {:answer/id #uuid "495a29d4-4685-53f5-aa7e-aca0f6ac95c8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378846} {:answer/id #uuid "6d50ad2d-de44-5bce-ac91-07540c84fecb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378847}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "29ff2373-e25a-5d6b-afc4-878204b60ffd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -5 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378844} :answer-field/id #uuid "ebf6e9b5-2957-558f-b65c-afc7fc8c7781" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378842}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d1a0662d-e8a7-5875-9a37-6a8d79742ba6" :question/math-academy-id "q-126752" :question/problem "Find a vector equation of the line that passes through the points $P(0,1,3)$ and $Q(3,-4,-2).$" :question/worked-solution "The vector equation of the straight line passing through $P$ and parallel to $v$ is given by\n\n$$\nr=p+tv,\n$$\n\nwhere $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )$ and $p$ is the position vector of $P.$ \n\nWe can find a direction vector by computing the displacement vector between the given points $P(0,1,3)$ and $Q(3,-4,-2)$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\overset{\\to }{PQ} \\\\  & =⟨3,-4,-2⟩-⟨0,1,3⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3,-5,-5⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the vector equation of the line is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -5 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186378848 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c338d1eb-7e13-5089-8dd3-d5ca6eefd4ba" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Points on a Line That Are a Fixed Distance From Another Point on the Line"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0f43cf15-1614-5176-91fd-0190558ca9f9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${A}_{1}(2,1,-2)$ and ${A}_{2}(4,1,1)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378850} {:answer/id #uuid "dbc09c5d-6029-5a07-98db-413f053b8d51" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${A}_{1}(2,1,3)$ and ${A}_{2}(2,-1,1)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378851} {:answer/id #uuid "3920fd72-1d12-5251-becb-545e8a78824a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${A}_{1}(2,1,3)$ and ${A}_{2}(4,1,-1)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378852} {:answer/id #uuid "836af86a-00c6-5b9a-a8fa-b4107cabb460" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${A}_{1}(2,1,3)$ and ${A}_{2}(1,2,-1)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378853} {:answer/id #uuid "9f98b808-f675-5036-8094-b312b168a7bc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${A}_{1}(1,2,3)$ and ${A}_{2}(4,1,-1)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378854}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3920fd72-1d12-5251-becb-545e8a78824a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${A}_{1}(2,1,3)$ and ${A}_{2}(4,1,-1)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378852} :answer-field/id #uuid "4744e544-4c7a-5dd4-ab0a-09c5f18432cc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378849}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "9cdad390-9975-5637-84b8-1dc45af58338" :question/math-academy-id "q-126991" :question/problem "Consider the straight line that passes through $P(3,1,1)$ and is parallel to $v=⟨-1,0,2⟩.$ Find all the possible points $A$ on that line such that $AP=\\sqrt{5}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the vector equation of the line, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =p+tv \\\\ r & =⟨3,1,1⟩+t⟨-1,0,2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\nSince $A$ lies on the line, we know that there must be a real number $t$ such that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{OA} & =⟨3,1,1⟩+t⟨-1,0,2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PA} & =\\overset{\\to }{OA}-\\overset{\\to }{OP} \\\\  & =(⟨3,1,1⟩+t⟨-1,0,2⟩)-⟨3,1,1⟩ \\\\  & =t\\,⟨-1,0,2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-t,\\,0,\\,2t⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the fact that $PA=\\sqrt{5},$ we get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AP & =\\sqrt{5} \\\\ |\\overset{\\to }{PA}| & =\\sqrt{5} \\\\ |⟨-t,\\,0,\\,2t⟩| & =\\sqrt{5} \\\\ \\sqrt{(-t)^{2}+(0)^{2}+(2t)^{2}} & =\\sqrt{5} \\\\ \\sqrt{{t}^{2}+0+4{t}^{2}} & =\\sqrt{5} \\\\ \\sqrt{5{t}^{2}} & =\\sqrt{5} \\\\ \\pm \\sqrt{5}t & =\\sqrt{5} \\\\ t & =\\pm 1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, putting the values $t=\\pm 1$ into the equation for the line, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\overset{\\to }{O{A}_{1}}=⟨3,1,1⟩+⟨-1,0,2⟩=⟨2,1,3⟩, \\\\  & \\overset{\\to }{O{A}_{2}}=⟨3,1,1⟩-⟨-1,0,2⟩=⟨4,1,-1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the points are ${A}_{1}(2,1,3)$ and ${A}_{2}(4,1,-1).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186311111 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c338d1eb-7e13-5089-8dd3-d5ca6eefd4ba" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Points on a Line That Are a Fixed Distance From Another Point on the Line"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bb34a150-e343-5f14-b288-386875381a71" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${A}_{1}(1,2,5)$ and ${A}_{2}(-5,3,1)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311113} {:answer/id #uuid "c8456756-54ca-592c-a289-99edc3aa3d7b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${A}_{1}(1,-1,-5)$ and ${A}_{2}(5,3,2)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311114} {:answer/id #uuid "a406d08d-e6bb-5c61-8aad-1593b1da44c0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${A}_{1}(1,1,-5)$ and ${A}_{2}(5,3,2)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311115} {:answer/id #uuid "2c9c966a-5aed-50c4-b30e-c9cc186fe8a9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${A}_{1}(1,-1,5)$ and ${A}_{2}(5,-3,1)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311116} {:answer/id #uuid "641b04fa-ffe5-5154-b59c-31c024713831" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${A}_{1}(-1,-1,5)$ and ${A}_{2}(4,-3,-1)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311117}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2c9c966a-5aed-50c4-b30e-c9cc186fe8a9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${A}_{1}(1,-1,5)$ and ${A}_{2}(5,-3,1)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311116} :answer-field/id #uuid "34a23037-a100-5f54-85a7-3c0b9303e5a7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311112}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "cbeb3212-31dc-5cc0-971a-bf4846f229e5" :question/math-academy-id "q-126992" :question/problem "Consider the straight line that passes through $P(3,-2,3)$ and is parallel to $v=⟨-2,1,2⟩.$ Find all the possible points $A$ on that line such that $AP=3.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the vector equation of the line, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =p+tv \\\\ r & =⟨3,-2,3⟩+t⟨-2,1,2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\nSince $A$ lies on the line, we know that there must be a real number $t$ such that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{OA} & =⟨3,-2,3⟩+t⟨-2,1,2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PA} & =\\overset{\\to }{OA}-\\overset{\\to }{OP} \\\\  & =(⟨3,-2,3⟩+t⟨-2,1,2⟩)-⟨3,-2,3⟩ \\\\  & =t\\,⟨-2,1,2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-2t,\\,t,\\,2t⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the fact that $PA=3,$ we get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AP & =3 \\\\ |\\overset{\\to }{PA}| & =3 \\\\ |⟨-2t,\\,t,\\,2t⟩| & =3 \\\\ \\sqrt{(-2t)^{2}+{t}^{2}+(2t)^{2}} & =3 \\\\ \\sqrt{4{t}^{2}+{t}^{2}+4{t}^{2}} & =3 \\\\ \\sqrt{9{t}^{2}} & =3 \\\\ \\pm 3t & =3 \\\\ t & =\\pm 1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, putting the values $t=\\pm 1$ into the equation for the line, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\overset{\\to }{O{A}_{1}}=⟨3,-2,3⟩+⟨-2,1,2⟩=⟨1,-1,5⟩, \\\\  & \\overset{\\to }{O{A}_{2}}=⟨3,-2,3⟩-⟨-2,1,2⟩=⟨5,-3,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the points are ${A}_{1}(1,-1,5)$ and ${A}_{2}(5,-3,1).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186311118 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c338d1eb-7e13-5089-8dd3-d5ca6eefd4ba" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Points on a Line That Are a Fixed Distance From Another Point on the Line"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f9a26130-b9ff-57cc-bb11-c79826a6b802" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${A}_{1}(1,-1,-7)$ and ${A}_{2}(5,5,5)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311120} {:answer/id #uuid "52dede04-bba1-5c39-a410-2592c55d3b76" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${A}_{1}(-1,1,7)$ and ${A}_{2}(5,5,5)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311121} {:answer/id #uuid "e4e62b70-6be7-5357-9bca-77c48e37e961" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${A}_{1}(-1,-1,7)$ and ${A}_{2}(5,-5,5)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311122} {:answer/id #uuid "f3804c30-94da-5f7a-b59b-deffb0ce5f3f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${A}_{1}(1,1,7)$ and ${A}_{2}(5,-5,5)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311123} {:answer/id #uuid "6eb5cfbc-22c3-528a-a30a-5c064ab2aa50" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${A}_{1}(-1,1,-7)$ and ${A}_{2}(5,5,5)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311124}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "52dede04-bba1-5c39-a410-2592c55d3b76" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${A}_{1}(-1,1,7)$ and ${A}_{2}(5,5,5)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311121} :answer-field/id #uuid "767e4e2d-0457-5fea-a1d0-540a9ba8e186" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311119}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "59a52ddc-339d-53d5-a5c4-8b8787ceb738" :question/math-academy-id "q-126995" :question/problem "Consider the straight line that passes through $P(2,3,6)$ and is parallel to $v=⟨-3,-2,1⟩.$ Find all the possible points $A$ on that line such that $AP=\\sqrt{14}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the vector equation of the line, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =p+tv \\\\ r & =⟨2,3,6⟩+t⟨-3,-2,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\nSince $A$ lies on the line, we know that there must be a real number $t$ such that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{OA} & =⟨2,3,6⟩+t⟨-3,-2,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PA} & =\\overset{\\to }{OA}-\\overset{\\to }{OP} \\\\  & =(⟨2,3,6⟩+t⟨-3,-2,1⟩)-⟨2,3,6⟩ \\\\  & =t\\,⟨-3,-2,1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-3t,\\,-2t,\\,t⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the fact that $PA=\\sqrt{14},$ we get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AP & =\\sqrt{14} \\\\ |\\overset{\\to }{PA}| & =\\sqrt{14} \\\\ |⟨-3t,\\,-2t,\\,t⟩| & =\\sqrt{14} \\\\ \\sqrt{(-3t)^{2}+(-2t)^{2}+{t}^{2}} & =\\sqrt{14} \\\\ \\sqrt{9{t}^{2}+4{t}^{2}+{t}^{2}} & =\\sqrt{14} \\\\ \\pm t\\sqrt{14} & =\\sqrt{14} \\\\ t & =\\pm 1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, putting the values $t=\\pm 1$ into the equation for the line, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\overset{\\to }{O{A}_{1}}=⟨2,3,6⟩+⟨-3,-2,1⟩=⟨-1,1,7⟩, \\\\  & \\overset{\\to }{O{A}_{2}}=⟨2,3,6⟩-⟨-3,-2,1⟩=⟨5,5,5⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the points are ${A}_{1}(-1,1,7)$ and ${A}_{2}(5,5,5).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186378855 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f78fe749-e37e-53f2-879f-4c36931c1d6f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Vector Equation of a Line Segment"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bb720808-7f35-5615-afa5-6d43cbbd150c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378857} {:answer/id #uuid "ee08904c-1ca6-5ec9-8491-6f0fb337106b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378858} {:answer/id #uuid "6e9ef99c-866d-5c0a-a537-23721ae5d96d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378859} {:answer/id #uuid "ddb8b6e2-3cf8-5294-bd42-8d8c52464407" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378860} {:answer/id #uuid "194fb037-0dcc-591f-8d97-af54ea4d1008" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378861}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bb720808-7f35-5615-afa5-6d43cbbd150c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378857} :answer-field/id #uuid "00c51068-485c-516a-ab41-fa42d16f690a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378856}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "3655f8c4-6353-513d-87a6-488985fb6d1d" :question/math-academy-id "q-162165" :question/problem "The equation below describes all the points on the line segment $\\overset{―}{PQ},$ where $P(0,-2,2)$ and $Q(1,-1,1).$\n\n$$\nr(t)=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -2 \\\\ a\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ b \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in [c,1]\n$$\n\nWhat is the value of $a+b+c?$" :question/worked-solution "We need to find a direction vector that is parallel to the given line. We can use the vector $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\overset{\\to }{PQ} \\\\  & =\\overset{\\to }{OQ}-\\overset{\\to }{OP} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the vector equation of the line is\n\n$$\nr=p+tv\\,⟹\\,r=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nand the vector equation of the line segment $\\overset{―}{PQ}$ is\n\n$$\nr(t)=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in [0,1].\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\na+b+c=2+1+0=3.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186378862 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f78fe749-e37e-53f2-879f-4c36931c1d6f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Vector Equation of a Line Segment"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fc74f0e0-fc8f-5dbe-bdd0-5900f8e29506" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378864} {:answer/id #uuid "8d7bb365-a917-5664-8269-7bc5da7e7b1e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378865} {:answer/id #uuid "20f7b68c-6ab8-55d6-8ed0-e8bb2f331c5a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378866} {:answer/id #uuid "78f1ff86-1800-5d64-b59d-7149e6b16549" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378867} {:answer/id #uuid "f090e232-7826-5453-b7ec-1660f21e1b1a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378868}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f090e232-7826-5453-b7ec-1660f21e1b1a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378868} :answer-field/id #uuid "734bb91b-30b0-5993-86f7-2020f626cc91" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378863}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "caa517c4-da2b-5132-bd37-7e3350606745" :question/math-academy-id "q-162167" :question/problem "The equation below describes all the points on the line segment $\\overset{―}{PQ},$ where $P(-3,5,0)$ and $Q(0,-3,2).$\n\n$$\nr(t)=[\\begin{aligned}a \\\\ 5 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -8 \\\\ b\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in [c,1]\n$$\n\nWhat is the value of $a+b+c?$" :question/worked-solution "We need to find a direction vector that is parallel to the given line. We can use the vector $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\overset{\\to }{PQ} \\\\  & =\\overset{\\to }{OQ}-\\overset{\\to }{OP} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -8 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the vector equation of the line is\n\n$$\nr=p+tv\\,⟹\\,r=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -8 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nand the vector equation of the  line segment $\\overset{―}{PQ}$ is\n\n$$\nr(t)=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -8 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in [0,1].\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\na+b+c=(-3)+2+0=-1.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186311132 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f78fe749-e37e-53f2-879f-4c36931c1d6f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Vector Equation of a Line Segment"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "85617a24-64b7-5da1-9338-83bce6bbcd63" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311134} {:answer/id #uuid "8d0147ca-bcd1-583b-ad66-678a590c7e05" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311135} {:answer/id #uuid "bf3e2f1d-ced2-5713-977d-d3119e1b264e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311136} {:answer/id #uuid "ebc57ed6-6e6e-51ee-95b3-3a3319fe89a3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311137} {:answer/id #uuid "c57adfc5-5ef8-51f2-8585-960b427e6ad1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311138}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "85617a24-64b7-5da1-9338-83bce6bbcd63" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311134} :answer-field/id #uuid "40261d74-6aea-550b-97b3-972cdc7008f6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311133}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "12c5ba63-0750-5dc9-b617-46b3345e0ebe" :question/math-academy-id "q-162169" :question/problem "The equation below describes all the points on the line segment $\\overset{―}{PQ},$ where $P(5,0,4)$ and $Q(-3,1,5).$\n\n$$\nr(t)=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ a \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}-8 \\\\ 1 \\\\ b\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in [0,c]\n$$\n\nWhat is the value of $a+b+c?$" :question/worked-solution "We need to find a direction vector that is parallel to the given line. We can use the vector $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\overset{\\to }{PQ} \\\\  & =\\overset{\\to }{OQ}-\\overset{\\to }{OP} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-8 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the vector equation of the line is\n\n$$\nr=p+tv\\,⟹\\,r=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}-8 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nand the vector equation of the  line segment $\\overset{―}{PQ}$ is\n\n$$\nr(t)=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}-8 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in [0,1].\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\na+b+c=0+1+1=2.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186378869 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f78fe749-e37e-53f2-879f-4c36931c1d6f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Vector Equation of a Line Segment"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d834feff-2792-5b70-8fab-c216cab7971d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3t+2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378871} {:answer/id #uuid "c0f6ab07-c4ed-568f-ad0c-e82f0d6cf69b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378872} {:answer/id #uuid "02a88889-2b7f-5907-a93c-0ada2125c7f8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "t+1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378873} {:answer/id #uuid "09563df0-8da1-5d05-9157-7a0ece50e1c6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378874} {:answer/id #uuid "77a65bb8-9d52-560d-92f2-7fbca81e4355" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1-4t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378875}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "09563df0-8da1-5d05-9157-7a0ece50e1c6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378874} :answer-field/id #uuid "60c33f77-559d-5666-886b-3d0d057cc1b0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378870}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f5b67e35-6407-5675-9c62-eeda9220de7a" :question/math-academy-id "q-162189" :question/problem "The equation below gives a parametrization of the line segment $\\overset{―}{PQ},$ where $P(1,-1,1)$ and $Q(2,-3,0).$\n\n$$\nr(t)=a\\,i-(2t+1)\\,j+b\\,k,\\,t\\in [c,1]\n$$\n\nWhat is $a+b+c?$" :question/worked-solution "We need to find a direction vector that is parallel to the given line. We can use the vector $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\overset{\\to }{PQ} \\\\  & =\\overset{\\to }{OQ}-\\overset{\\to }{OP} \\\\  & =(2\\,i-3\\,j)-(i-j+k) \\\\  & =i-2\\,j-k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the vector equation of the line is\n\n$$\nr=p+tv\\,⟹\\,r=(i-j+k)+t(i-2\\,j-k)\n$$\n\nand the parametrization of the line segment $\\overset{―}{PQ}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t) & =(i-j+k)+t(i-2\\,j-k) \\\\  & =(t+1)\\,i-(2t+1)\\,j+(1-t)\\,k,\\,t\\in [0,1].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\na+b+c=(t+1)+(1-t)+0=2.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186378876 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f78fe749-e37e-53f2-879f-4c36931c1d6f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Vector Equation of a Line Segment"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ee1d537b-0f12-5db5-ba10-dd18638a99c3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10-2t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378878} {:answer/id #uuid "e628fbeb-7adc-5e13-af47-b6d8e6d7979c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378879} {:answer/id #uuid "aca5a0ae-13ba-53f8-aa5a-2d63f86d08a1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9-4t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378880} {:answer/id #uuid "a11421e4-f7ce-56ed-8242-6dcf32e1f645" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378881} {:answer/id #uuid "29e6c43f-3c5f-5d68-b5a7-49e1dcedb3e8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2t+8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378882}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "aca5a0ae-13ba-53f8-aa5a-2d63f86d08a1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9-4t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378880} :answer-field/id #uuid "12d8c907-c448-501d-91ec-9c238b128ab8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378877}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "ced958ce-3e6a-547a-bcd1-c688c5858ff2" :question/math-academy-id "q-162191" :question/problem "The equation below gives a parametrization of the line segment $\\overset{―}{PQ},$ where $P(4,3,5)$ and $Q(6,3,1).$\n\n$$\nr(t)=(2t+4)\\,i+a\\,j+b\\,k,\\,t\\in [0,c]\n$$\n\nWhat is $a+b+c?$" :question/worked-solution "We need to find a direction vector that is parallel to the given line. We can use the vector $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\overset{\\to }{PQ} \\\\  & =\\overset{\\to }{OQ}-\\overset{\\to }{OP} \\\\  & =(6\\,i+3\\,j+k)-(4\\,i+3\\,j+5\\,k) \\\\  & =2\\,i-4\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the vector equation of the line is\n\n$$\nr=p+tv\\,⟹\\,r=(4\\,i+3\\,j+5\\,k)+t(2\\,i-4\\,k)\n$$\n\nand the parametrization of the line segment $\\overset{―}{PQ}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t) & =(4\\,i+3\\,j+5\\,k)+t(2\\,i-4\\,k) \\\\  & =(2t+4)\\,i+3\\,j+(5-4t)\\,k,\\,t\\in [0,1].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\na+b+c=3+(5-4t)+1=9-4t.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186378883 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a6dee200-f517-5645-87ec-ccf36012e55e" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Vector Equation of the Line Passing Through Two Given Points"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8c69a302-8d7a-5878-a364-7274988835ff" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378885} {:answer/id #uuid "5200189f-b768-5d91-9a71-84741151637b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378886} {:answer/id #uuid "f9cbb1c1-b3d9-52bf-8a6b-80077851fcfb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 11\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378887} {:answer/id #uuid "35a1413a-ff4a-5190-940a-9b3ae148541c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378888} {:answer/id #uuid "c360d021-45c1-51c7-aa38-5d0b1eff2d97" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378889}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "35a1413a-ff4a-5190-940a-9b3ae148541c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378888} :answer-field/id #uuid "43b2a368-4618-598a-8ed2-2b0f4f4f4f1b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378884}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "9116d22e-f87b-5864-86ba-f50fe7056c3a" :question/math-academy-id "q-22317" :question/problem "Find a vector equation of the line that passes through the points $C(3,2,5)$ and $D(2,1,6).$" :question/worked-solution "The vector equation of the straight line passing through $C$ and parallel to $v$ is given by\n\n$$\nr=c+tv,\n$$\n\nwhere $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )$ and $c$ is the position vector of $C.$ \n\nWe can find a direction vector by computing the displacement vector between the given points $C(3,2,5)$ and $D(2,1,6)$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\overset{\\to }{CD} \\\\  & =⟨2,1,6⟩-⟨3,2,5⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-1,-1,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the vector equation of the line is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186378890 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "dcf425bc-d6ce-5cab-87ea-2d4d42270d09" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Vector Equation of a Line Given a Point and Direction Vector"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "98b95f30-daf2-565b-adf9-dc13c3a6600b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ -4 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378892} {:answer/id #uuid "81a30b95-d3c9-51f4-9ed5-3039f3115c72" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ -4 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378893} {:answer/id #uuid "801d6f55-e936-5c91-ad75-bbf4dde678f8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ -5 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378894} {:answer/id #uuid "695b553f-56a1-5773-b10c-ece1e80c28c1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ -4 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378895} {:answer/id #uuid "06577cc7-3658-5d2c-98df-44daf04f768d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ -4 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378896}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "81a30b95-d3c9-51f4-9ed5-3039f3115c72" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ -4 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378893} :answer-field/id #uuid "c47384e0-bc79-501c-801c-276a217a9c5c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378891}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "8325700c-fafc-5985-a379-0bbaab24164d" :question/math-academy-id "q-35962" :question/problem "Find a vector equation of the straight line passing through $P(-3,-4,-5)$ and parallel to $v=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "The vector equation of the straight line passing through $P$ and parallel to $v$ is given by\n\n$$\nr=p+tv,\n$$\n\nwhere $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )$ and $p$ is the position vector of $P.$\n\nIn our case, the position vector of the point $P$ is $p=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ -4 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}].$\n\nUsing the formula for the vector equation of a line, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ -4 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186311174 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "dcf425bc-d6ce-5cab-87ea-2d4d42270d09" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Vector Equation of a Line Given a Point and Direction Vector"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "26ddaaa1-51e9-5256-8ec2-61b60dbea226" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨-3,3,3⟩+⟨\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3},-5,3⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311176} {:answer/id #uuid "b5dde3bd-6987-5975-9067-1e687e3b1c3d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨3,-3,3⟩+t⟨\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3},3,-5⟩,\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311177} {:answer/id #uuid "bea8ca7c-c0d4-50e3-85ae-c87e5205c673" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨-5,3,\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3}⟩+t⟨3,3,-3⟩,\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311178} {:answer/id #uuid "653bf4c9-c0a3-559c-9e86-26f8847fa2f0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3},-5,3⟩+t⟨-3,3,3⟩,\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311179} {:answer/id #uuid "9ca224dd-5998-560d-aa59-8614d17185e9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨-3,3,3⟩+t⟨\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3},-5,3⟩,\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311180}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9ca224dd-5998-560d-aa59-8614d17185e9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨-3,3,3⟩+t⟨\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3},-5,3⟩,\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311180} :answer-field/id #uuid "709b2df5-e690-57c3-b850-b19b6bbfc11a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 1759