nding a Vector Equation of a Line Given a Point and Direction Vector"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7dc134a5-bb7d-5816-8a46-8637f00fd473" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨0,-\\sqrt{5},-1⟩+⟨5,5,-5⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378905} {:answer/id #uuid "723c4f78-e7d1-5280-a826-409853d8818b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨0,-\\sqrt{5},-1⟩+t⟨5,5,-5⟩,\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378906} {:answer/id #uuid "6d199019-9df7-5d7c-9b5b-76bfdb57dd28" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨5,5,-5⟩+t⟨0,-\\sqrt{5},-1⟩,\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378907} {:answer/id #uuid "49823e11-86c6-5c1f-b904-422db598f874" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨-5,5,5⟩+t⟨-1,-\\sqrt{5},0⟩,\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378908} {:answer/id #uuid "45b0f036-0c41-5a4d-92d4-0b0441c52f8a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨0,-1,-\\sqrt{5}⟩+t⟨5,-5,5⟩,\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378909}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6d199019-9df7-5d7c-9b5b-76bfdb57dd28" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨5,5,-5⟩+t⟨0,-\\sqrt{5},-1⟩,\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378907} :answer-field/id #uuid "ebe49f10-2906-5f77-83b1-7088dac02e05" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378904}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "40c286e5-b8a3-503b-95ec-4dac358498af" :question/math-academy-id "q-35968" :question/problem "Find a vector equation of the straight line passing through $P(5,5,-5)$ and parallel to $v=⟨0,-\\sqrt{5},-1⟩.$" :question/worked-solution "The vector equation of the straight line passing through $P$ and parallel to $v$ is given by\n\n$$\nr=p+tv,\n$$\n\nwhere $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )$ and $p$ is the position vector of $P.$\n\nIn our case, the position vector of the point $P$ is $p=⟨5,5,-5⟩.$\n\nUsing the formula for the vector equation of a line, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r=⟨5,5,-5⟩+t⟨0,-\\sqrt{5},-1⟩,\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186106214 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a6dee200-f517-5645-87ec-ccf36012e55e" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Vector Equation of the Line Passing Through Two Given Points"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2b00f4bc-4c40-535d-97af-f52369d212b5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378911} {:answer/id #uuid "b316decd-3957-55ec-9a96-e4b2b214ab4d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ -3 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378912} {:answer/id #uuid "8b08df02-ec6b-54f3-bc38-1b13534b2c57" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ -3 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378913} {:answer/id #uuid "64fc9283-cab9-51bc-be23-25d1cd96bcda" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378914} {:answer/id #uuid "d8f02f12-9285-59bc-9c82-83ad34cd9a0b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378915}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b316decd-3957-55ec-9a96-e4b2b214ab4d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ -3 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378912} :answer-field/id #uuid "c640ac25-59b6-5508-960f-c2bc379c3546" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378910}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "3ed6737a-6704-5d6d-9ae9-04e0ade520fe" :question/math-academy-id "q-35973" :question/problem "Find a vector equation of the line that passes through the points $A(4,5,3)$ and $B(-1,2,0).$" :question/worked-solution "The vector equation of the straight line passing through $A$ and parallel to $v$ is given by\n\n$$\nr=a+tv,\n$$\n\nwhere $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )$ and $a$ is the position vector of $A.$ \n\nWe can find a direction vector by computing the displacement vector between the given points $A(4,5,3)$ and $B(-1,2,0)$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\overset{\\to }{AB} \\\\  & =⟨-1,2,0⟩-⟨4,5,3⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-5,-3,-3⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the vector equation of the line is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ -3 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186311187 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a6dee200-f517-5645-87ec-ccf36012e55e" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Vector Equation of the Line Passing Through Two Given Points"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "03bb1d80-0e09-5279-ba61-e3b34b1934f6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ -3 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311189} {:answer/id #uuid "3a3de85a-798b-573f-aad2-4cd3b7bca002" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311190} {:answer/id #uuid "b030f7d5-dd54-5e2a-ad3e-f51a1bf0dabc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ -3 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311191} {:answer/id #uuid "1ce76003-0b7a-50b2-b3a2-fd15f4845c69" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311192} {:answer/id #uuid "1ba33e16-89dd-5424-9ffc-a5c450f1db01" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ -3 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311193}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b030f7d5-dd54-5e2a-ad3e-f51a1bf0dabc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ -3 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311191} :answer-field/id #uuid "1ff96cd7-3685-5fde-ab5c-d93df5715d3d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311188}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "1b5b7d76-7995-5fd2-be2e-9a59c7b1bd88" :question/math-academy-id "q-69772" :question/problem "Find a vector equation of the line that passes through the points $K(-4,-3,-1)$ and $L(1,2,4).$" :question/worked-solution "The vector equation of the straight line passing through $K$ and parallel to $v$ is given by\n\n$$\nr=k+tv,\n$$\n\nwhere $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )$ and $k$ is the position vector of $K.$ \n\nWe can find a direction vector by computing the displacement vector between the given points $K(-4,-3,-1)$ and $L(1,2,4),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\overset{\\to }{KL} \\\\  & =⟨1,2,4⟩-⟨-4,-3,-1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨5,5,5⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the vector equation of the line is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ -3 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186378916 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a6dee200-f517-5645-87ec-ccf36012e55e" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Vector Equation of the Line Passing Through Two Given Points"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1953663d-ab90-50f6-b08e-653bfe3446df" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 7 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378918} {:answer/id #uuid "36d8115c-bc43-5724-83b7-4520a32f47a3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 7 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378919} {:answer/id #uuid "5cdb49fa-d1fe-51c5-8858-02e190fac073" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378920} {:answer/id #uuid "484d9fd6-a59b-59bb-9270-d5de5473dd11" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 7 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378921} {:answer/id #uuid "90894d0b-7cad-5552-839d-9145be534991" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378922}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "36d8115c-bc43-5724-83b7-4520a32f47a3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 7 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378919} :answer-field/id #uuid "a0373824-e32c-5e43-b21a-847d8420e64d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378917}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "de330e5d-d3af-5611-ac93-1e08d17f5215" :question/math-academy-id "q-69773" :question/problem "Find a vector equation of the line that passes through the points $H(5,7,2)$ and $S(3,4,5).$" :question/worked-solution "The vector equation of the straight line passing through $H$ and parallel to $v$ is given by\n\n$$\nr=h+tv,\n$$\n\nwhere $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )$ and $h$ is the position vector of $H.$ \n\nWe can find a direction vector by computing the displacement vector between the given points $H(5,7,2)$ and $S(3,4,5),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\overset{\\to }{HS} \\\\  & =⟨3,4,5⟩-⟨5,7,2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-2,-3,3⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the vector equation of the line is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 7 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186378923 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c338d1eb-7e13-5089-8dd3-d5ca6eefd4ba" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Points on a Line That Are a Fixed Distance From Another Point on the Line"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "65192396-8117-5ac1-9ad7-8f14f0739b85" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${R}_{1}(4,-3,-3)$ and ${R}_{2}(2,3,3)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378925} {:answer/id #uuid "1979ade1-f969-5234-a158-d6470ebfe2d4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${R}_{1}(4,2,2)$ and ${R}_{2}(-3,-2,-2)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378926} {:answer/id #uuid "488a2399-f007-5a8c-9158-0bf0e82e756e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${R}_{1}(4,3,3)$ and ${R}_{2}(2,3,3)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378927} {:answer/id #uuid "ddc3d0d9-fb76-5ad6-aefc-a56753d8a6d1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${R}_{1}(4,3,3)$ and ${R}_{2}(-2,-3,-3)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378928} {:answer/id #uuid "8d512922-7757-5d7c-8898-f3d5eb89a246" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${R}_{1}(3,4,4)$ and ${R}_{2}(3,-2,-2)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378929}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ddc3d0d9-fb76-5ad6-aefc-a56753d8a6d1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${R}_{1}(4,3,3)$ and ${R}_{2}(-2,-3,-3)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378928} :answer-field/id #uuid "7ddc2ced-aa2d-5c15-93e6-d0565dec45fd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378924}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "2efe9b2b-7d22-5f68-b28a-0c83a296200e" :question/math-academy-id "q-69783" :question/problem "Consider the straight line that passes through $P(1,0,0)$ and is parallel to $v=⟨1,1,1⟩.$ Find all the possible points $R$ on that line such that $RP=3\\sqrt{3}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the vector equation of the line, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =p+tv \\\\ r & =⟨1,0,0⟩+t⟨1,1,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\nSince $R$ lies on the line, we know that there must be a real number $t$ such that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{OR} & =⟨1,0,0⟩+t⟨1,1,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PR} & =\\overset{\\to }{OR}-\\overset{\\to }{OP} \\\\  & =(⟨1,0,0⟩+t⟨1,1,1⟩)-⟨1,0,0⟩ \\\\  & =t\\,⟨1,1,1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨t,\\,t,\\,t⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the fact that $PR=3\\sqrt{3},$ we get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}RP & =3\\sqrt{3} \\\\ |\\overset{\\to }{PR}| & =3\\sqrt{3} \\\\ |⟨t,\\,t,\\,t⟩| & =3\\sqrt{3} \\\\ \\sqrt{{t}^{2}+{t}^{2}+{t}^{2}} & =3\\sqrt{3} \\\\ \\sqrt{3{t}^{2}} & =3\\sqrt{3} \\\\ \\pm t\\sqrt{3} & =3\\sqrt{3} \\\\ t & =\\pm 3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, putting the values $t=\\pm 3$ into the equation for the line, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\overset{\\to }{O{R}_{1}}=⟨1,0,0⟩+3⟨1,1,1⟩=⟨4,3,3⟩, \\\\  & \\overset{\\to }{O{R}_{2}}=⟨1,0,0⟩-3⟨1,1,1⟩=⟨-2,-3,-3⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the points are ${R}_{1}(4,3,3)$ and ${R}_{2}(-2,-3,-3).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186311215 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c338d1eb-7e13-5089-8dd3-d5ca6eefd4ba" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Points on a Line That Are a Fixed Distance From Another Point on the Line"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "00372776-9900-5873-b2d8-8af723760951" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${Q}_{1}(6,2,2)$ and ${Q}_{2}(1,0,-2)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311217} {:answer/id #uuid "e54b1804-49df-5963-bd11-66814707531f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${Q}_{1}(4,2,6)$ and ${Q}_{2}(1,0,2)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311218} {:answer/id #uuid "2aaa7882-74d1-5f0e-a190-932cda76b670" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${Q}_{1}(2,0,6)$ and ${Q}_{2}(0,2,-4)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311219} {:answer/id #uuid "f00c74ee-9fcf-54b1-97e8-a6bac73a5b5e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${Q}_{1}(2,0,6)$ and ${Q}_{2}(-1,3,-9)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311220} {:answer/id #uuid "0cc8c193-62df-53c3-8f7c-bc7b22d80f1b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${Q}_{1}(3,-1,11)$ and ${Q}_{2}(0,2,-4)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311221}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2aaa7882-74d1-5f0e-a190-932cda76b670" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${Q}_{1}(2,0,6)$ and ${Q}_{2}(0,2,-4)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311219} :answer-field/id #uuid "13bc0196-3911-5c03-a822-6873c92903a5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311216}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "ca1265ac-23c6-5e5b-be9c-b56a47160343" :question/math-academy-id "q-77443" :question/problem "Consider the straight line that passes through $P(1,1,1)$ and is parallel to $v=⟨1,-1,5⟩.$ Find all the possible points $Q$ on that line such that $PQ=3\\sqrt{3}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the vector equation of the line, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =p+tv \\\\ r & =⟨1,1,1⟩+t⟨1,-1,5⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\nSince $Q$ lies on the line, we know that there must be a real number $t$ such that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{OQ} & =⟨1,1,1⟩+t⟨1,-1,5⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =\\overset{\\to }{OQ}-\\overset{\\to }{OP} \\\\  & =(⟨1,1,1⟩+t⟨1,-1,5⟩)-⟨1,1,1⟩ \\\\  & =t\\,⟨1,-1,5⟩ \\\\  & =⟨t,\\,-t,\\,5t⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the fact that $PQ=3\\sqrt{3},$ we get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}PQ & =3\\sqrt{3} \\\\ |\\overset{\\to }{PQ}| & =3\\sqrt{3} \\\\ |⟨t,\\,-t,\\,5t⟩| & =3\\sqrt{3} \\\\ \\sqrt{{t}^{2}+(-t)^{2}+(5t)^{2}} & =3\\sqrt{3} \\\\ \\sqrt{27{t}^{2}} & =3\\sqrt{3} \\\\ \\pm 3\\sqrt{3}t & =3\\sqrt{3} \\\\ t & =\\pm 1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, putting the values $t=\\pm 1$ into the equation for the line, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\overset{\\to }{O{Q}_{1}}=⟨1,1,1⟩+⟨1,-1,5⟩=⟨2,0,6⟩, \\\\  & \\overset{\\to }{O{Q}_{2}}=⟨1,1,1⟩-⟨1,-1,5⟩=⟨0,2,-4⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the points are ${Q}_{1}(2,0,6)$ and ${Q}_{2}(0,2,-4).$"}]}
